IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `dg-core`
IMPORT `dg2-support`

-- Delaware General Corporation Law, 8 Del. C. ch. 1: section 141(a), (b) and (j) -- THE BOARD OF DIRECTORS: who manages, its members,
-- their qualifications, terms and resignations, the quorum, the act of the board, and the reading for a nonstock corporation.
--
-- SEAT: a person who incorporates, directs or holds stock in a Delaware corporation. Rules here are layer 1: they take the
-- facts as plain inputs and decide what the text decides; the seat layer (dg2-seat.l4) asks them as that person would.
-- The source is the plain-text rendering de-code-t8-ch1-2026-10-01.txt (not the official text); `-- src:N | ...` quotes line N of it.
--
-- READING OF "total number of directors" (Fork F-141-1 in NOTES.md): the text says "a majority of the total number of directors"
-- (src:364) and, elsewhere, "a majority of the whole board" (src:365). This module takes `the total number of directors` as an
-- input and does not decide whether vacancies count; the seat asks for the full number of seats the board has.
-- COUNTS ARE VOTES (s 141(d), last sentence, src:369): where the certificate gives a director more or less than one vote, every
-- count of directors in this module is a count of the votes of the directors.
-- NOTE ON s 114: section 114(b)(1) takes section 141 out of the stockholder-to-member reading of section 114(a), because
-- section 141(j) makes that reading itself (see below).

§ `Section 141(a): who manages the business and affairs`

-- The three answers to "who manages?": the board (the default), someone this chapter names, or someone the certificate names.
-- src:363 | The business and affairs of every corporation organized under this chapter shall be managed by or under the direction of a board of directors, except as may be otherwise provided in this chapter or in its certificate of incorporation. …
-- src:363 | If any such provision is made in the certificate of incorporation, the powers and duties conferred or imposed upon the board of directors by this chapter shall be exercised or performed to such extent and by such person or persons as shall be provided in the certificate of incorporation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 141(a) (src:363)
DECLARE `s 141(a) Who manages the business and affairs` IS ONE OF
    `the board of directors, by itself or through those it directs, under s 141(a)`
    `the person or persons this chapter provides in place of the board, under s 141(a)`
    `the person or persons the certificate of incorporation provides in place of the board, under s 141(a)`

-- Where the certificate makes a provision, the powers and duties the chapter confers on the board are exercised by the
-- person or persons the certificate names (second sentence); otherwise, if the chapter itself provides otherwise, by whom the
-- chapter says; otherwise the board.
-- src:363 | The business and affairs of every corporation organized under this chapter shall be managed by or under the direction of a board of directors, except as may be otherwise provided in this chapter or in its certificate of incorporation. …
-- src:363 | If any such provision is made in the certificate of incorporation, the powers and duties conferred or imposed upon the board of directors by this chapter shall be exercised or performed to such extent and by such person or persons as shall be provided in the certificate of incorporation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 141(a) (src:363)
GIVEN `this chapter provides that someone other than the board manages the matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the certificate of incorporation provides that someone other than the board manages the matter` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 141(a) Who manages the business and affairs`
`s 141(a) who manages the business and affairs` `this chapter provides that someone other than the board manages the matter` `the certificate of incorporation provides that someone other than the board manages the matter` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the certificate of incorporation provides that someone other than the board manages the matter`
        THEN `the person or persons the certificate of incorporation provides in place of the board, under s 141(a)`
        IF `this chapter provides that someone other than the board manages the matter`
        THEN `the person or persons this chapter provides in place of the board, under s 141(a)`
        OTHERWISE `the board of directors, by itself or through those it directs, under s 141(a)`

§ `Section 141(b): members, qualifications, terms and resignation`

-- "The board of directors of a corporation shall consist of 1 or more members, each of whom shall be a natural person."
-- src:364 | The board of directors of a corporation shall consist of 1 or more members, each of whom shall be a natural person. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 141(b) (src:364)
GIVEN `the number of members of the board` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 141(b) the board consists of one or more members` `the number of members of the board` MEANS
    `the number of members of the board` AT LEAST 1

-- Only a natural person may be a member of the board; the core's `Kind of entity` has `a natural person` as its first constructor.
-- src:364 | each of whom shall be a natural person. The number of directors shall be fixed by, or in the manner provided in, the bylaws, unless the certificate of incorporation fixes the number of directors, in which case a change in the number of directors shall be made only by amendment of the certificate. Directors need not be stockholders unless so required by the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws. The certificate of incorporation or bylaws may prescribe other qualifications for directors. Each director shall hold office until such director’s successor is elected and qualified or until such director’s earlier resignation or removal. Any director may resign at any time upon notice given in writing or by electronic transmission to the corporation. A resignation is effective when the resignation is delivered unless the resignation specifies a later effective date or an effective date determined upon the happening of an event or events. A resignation which is conditioned upon the director failing to receive a specified vote for reelection as a director may provide that it is irrevocable. A majority of the total number of directors shall constitute a quorum for the transaction of business unless the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws require a greater number. Unless the certificate of incorporation provides otherwise, the bylaws may provide that a number less than a majority shall constitute a quorum which in no case shall be less than ⅓ of the total number of directors. The vote of the majority of the directors present at a meeting at which a quorum is present shall be the act of the board of directors unless the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws shall require a vote of a greater number.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 141(b) (src:364)
GIVEN `the kind of person` IS A `Kind of entity`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 141(b) a person of this kind may be a member of the board` `the kind of person` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the kind of person`
    WHEN `a natural person` THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

-- src:364 | The number of directors shall be fixed by, or in the manner provided in, the bylaws, unless the certificate of incorporation fixes the number of directors, in which case a change in the number of directors shall be made only by amendment of the certificate. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 141(b) (src:364)
DECLARE `s 141(b) How the number of directors is changed` IS ONE OF
    `in the manner provided in the bylaws`
    `only by amendment of the certificate of incorporation`

-- The bylaws fix the number or the manner of fixing it, unless the certificate fixes the number, in which case a change is made
-- only by amendment of the certificate.
-- src:364 | The number of directors shall be fixed by, or in the manner provided in, the bylaws, unless the certificate of incorporation fixes the number of directors, in which case a change in the number of directors shall be made only by amendment of the certificate. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 141(b) (src:364)
GIVEN `the certificate of incorporation fixes the number of directors` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `s 141(b) How the number of directors is changed`
`s 141(b) how the number of directors is changed` `the certificate of incorporation fixes the number of directors` MEANS
    IF   `the certificate of incorporation fixes the number of directors`
    THEN `only by amendment of the certificate of incorporation`
    ELSE `in the manner provided in the bylaws`

-- "Directors need not be stockholders unless so required by the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws."
-- A requirement said to be made anywhere else (a board resolution) is not one the text recognises.
-- src:364 | Directors need not be stockholders unless so required by the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 141(b) (src:364)
GIVEN `where the requirement that directors be stockholders is made` IS A `Where a provision is made`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 141(b) a director must be a stockholder` `where the requirement that directors be stockholders is made` MEANS
    `dg2 the place is the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws` `where the requirement that directors be stockholders is made`

-- "The certificate of incorporation or bylaws may prescribe other qualifications for directors."
-- src:364 | The certificate of incorporation or bylaws may prescribe other qualifications for directors. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 141(b) (src:364)
GIVEN `where the other qualification is prescribed` IS A `Where a provision is made`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 141(b) a qualification for directors prescribed there is one the Law allows` `where the other qualification is prescribed` MEANS
    `dg2 the place is the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws` `where the other qualification is prescribed`

-- The holdover rule: a director holds office until a successor is elected and qualified, or until the director's earlier
-- resignation or removal.
-- src:364 | Each director shall hold office until such director’s successor is elected and qualified or until such director’s earlier resignation or removal. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 141(b) (src:364)
GIVEN `a successor has been elected and has qualified` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the resignation has become effective` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the director has been removed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 141(b) the director still holds office` `a successor has been elected and has qualified` `the resignation has become effective` `the director has been removed` MEANS
    NOT (   `a successor has been elected and has qualified`
         OR `the resignation has become effective`
         OR `the director has been removed`)

-- Resignation: "upon notice given in writing or by electronic transmission to the corporation".
-- The definition of "electronic transmission" is section 232(d)(1) (piece dg5); here it is one fact.
-- out of range: section 232(d)(1) (piece dg5): "electronic transmission" is defined there; whether the notice is one is a plain fact here.
-- src:364 | Any director may resign at any time upon notice given in writing or by electronic transmission to the corporation. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 141(b) (src:364)
GIVEN `the notice is given to the corporation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice is in writing` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice is given by electronic transmission` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 141(b) the notice of resignation is in a form the Law allows` `the notice is given to the corporation` `the notice is in writing` `the notice is given by electronic transmission` MEANS
        `the notice is given to the corporation`
    AND (`the notice is in writing` OR `the notice is given by electronic transmission`)

DECLARE `s 141(b) Resignation` HAS
    `the date the notice of resignation is delivered to the corporation` IS A DATE
    `the later effective date the resignation specifies` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `the resignation specifies an effective date determined upon the happening of an event or events` IS A BOOLEAN
    `the date the event or events happen` IS A MAYBE DATE

-- "A resignation is effective when the resignation is delivered unless the resignation specifies a later effective date or an
-- effective date determined upon the happening of an event or events." NOTHING while an event-determined date has not yet come.
-- src:364 | A resignation is effective when the resignation is delivered unless the resignation specifies a later effective date or an effective date determined upon the happening of an event or events. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 141(b) (src:364)
GIVEN r IS A `s 141(b) Resignation`
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`s 141(b) the date the resignation is effective` r MEANS
    IF   r's `the resignation specifies an effective date determined upon the happening of an event or events`
    THEN r's `the date the event or events happen`
    ELSE CONSIDER r's `the later effective date the resignation specifies`
         WHEN JUST d THEN (IF d GREATER THAN delivered THEN JUST d ELSE JUST delivered)
         WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST delivered
    WHERE
        delivered MEANS r's `the date the notice of resignation is delivered to the corporation`

-- "A resignation which is conditioned upon the director failing to receive a specified vote for reelection as a director may
-- provide that it is irrevocable." For any other resignation the text does not say whether it may be made irrevocable.
-- src:364 | A resignation which is conditioned upon the director failing to receive a specified vote for reelection as a director may provide that it is irrevocable. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 141(b) (src:364)
GIVEN `the resignation is conditioned upon the director failing to receive a specified vote for reelection` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 141(b) the resignation may provide that it is irrevocable` `the resignation is conditioned upon the director failing to receive a specified vote for reelection` MEANS
    IF   `the resignation is conditioned upon the director failing to receive a specified vote for reelection`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

§ `Section 141(b): the quorum and the act of the board`

-- The base of the vote: "the total number of directors" (the core has no base of that name).
-- src:364 | A majority of the total number of directors shall constitute a quorum for the transaction of business unless the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws require a greater number. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 141(b) (src:364)
GIVETH A `Vote base`
`s 141(b) the total number of directors as a vote base` MEANS
    `another base named in the provision` "the total number of directors"

DECLARE `s 141(b) Quorum provisions` HAS
    `the total number of directors` IS A NUMBER
    `the number of directors the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws fix as a quorum` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `where that number is fixed` IS A `Where a provision is made`
    `the certificate of incorporation provides that the bylaws may not fix a smaller quorum` IS A BOOLEAN

-- The quorum, in the text's three layers:
--   * a majority of the total number of directors, unless the certificate or the bylaws require a greater number;
--   * "Unless the certificate of incorporation provides otherwise, the bylaws may provide that a number less than a majority
--     shall constitute a quorum which in no case shall be less than 1/3 of the total number of directors."
-- A number fixed in the certificate or the bylaws that is a majority or more is a greater (or equal) requirement. A number that is
-- not a majority is a smaller quorum: only the bylaws may fix it, only if the certificate does not provide otherwise, and never
-- below one third. Where the certificate itself fixes a smaller number, or the bylaws fix one below one third, the text does not
-- say what the quorum is: NOTHING. A number said to be fixed in a board resolution, or nowhere, is ignored: the majority stands.
-- src:364 | A majority of the total number of directors shall constitute a quorum for the transaction of business unless the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws require a greater number. …
-- src:364 | Unless the certificate of incorporation provides otherwise, the bylaws may provide that a number less than a majority shall constitute a quorum which in no case shall be less than ⅓ of the total number of directors. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 141(b) (src:364)
GIVEN q IS A `s 141(b) Quorum provisions`
GIVETH A MAYBE `Vote requirement`
`s 141(b) the quorum requirement` q MEANS
    IF   q's `the total number of directors` AT MOST 0
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER q's `the number of directors the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws fix as a quorum`
         WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST (`a majority of` `s 141(b) the total number of directors as a vote base`)
         WHEN JUST k THEN
             BRANCH
                 IF   NOT (`dg2 the place is the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws` (q's `where that number is fixed`))
                 THEN JUST (`a majority of` `s 141(b) the total number of directors as a vote base`)
                 IF   k AT MOST 0
                 THEN NOTHING
                 IF   k GREATER THAN (q's `the total number of directors` DIVIDED BY 2)
                 THEN (IF   k AT MOST q's `the total number of directors`
                       THEN JUST (`at least` (k DIVIDED BY q's `the total number of directors`) `of` `s 141(b) the total number of directors as a vote base`)
                       ELSE NOTHING)
                 IF   q's `where that number is fixed` EQUALS `in the certificate of incorporation`
                 THEN NOTHING
                 IF   q's `the certificate of incorporation provides that the bylaws may not fix a smaller quorum`
                 THEN JUST (`a majority of` `s 141(b) the total number of directors as a vote base`)
                 IF   k AT LEAST (q's `the total number of directors` DIVIDED BY 3)
                 THEN JUST (`at least` (k DIVIDED BY q's `the total number of directors`) `of` `s 141(b) the total number of directors as a vote base`)
                 OTHERWISE NOTHING

-- Is a quorum present? The number present is a count of directors (or of their votes: see the header). NOTHING where the
-- quorum requirement is not covered, or the counts cannot be a vote.
-- src:364 | A majority of the total number of directors shall constitute a quorum for the transaction of business …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 141(b) (src:364)
GIVEN `the number of directors present` IS A NUMBER
      q IS A `s 141(b) Quorum provisions`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 141(b) a quorum of the directors is present` `the number of directors present` q MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 141(b) the quorum requirement` q
    WHEN JUST r THEN `the vote carries` r `the number of directors present` (q's `the total number of directors`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING

DECLARE `s 141(b) Vote of the board` HAS
    `the number of directors present at the meeting` IS A NUMBER
    `the number of directors voting in favor` IS A NUMBER
    `where a vote of a greater number is required` IS A `Where a provision is made`
    `the greater number of directors required to vote in favor` IS A NUMBER

-- "The vote of the majority of the directors present at a meeting at which a quorum is present shall be the act of the board of
-- directors unless the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws shall require a vote of a greater number."
-- Fork F-141-2: without a quorum there is no act of the board (the quorum is "for the transaction of business").
-- src:364 | The vote of the majority of the directors present at a meeting at which a quorum is present shall be the act of the board of directors unless the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws shall require a vote of a greater number.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 141(b) (src:364)
GIVEN q IS A `s 141(b) Quorum provisions`
      v IS A `s 141(b) Vote of the board`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 141(b) the act of the board of directors is carried` q v MEANS
    `dg2 both findings hold`
        (`s 141(b) a quorum of the directors is present` (v's `the number of directors present at the meeting`) q)
        (`dg2 both findings hold`
            (`the vote carries`
                (`a majority of` `the directors present at a meeting at which a quorum is present`)
                (v's `the number of directors voting in favor`)
                (v's `the number of directors present at the meeting`))
            (IF   `dg2 the place is the certificate of incorporation or the bylaws` (v's `where a vote of a greater number is required`)
             THEN JUST (v's `the number of directors voting in favor` AT LEAST v's `the greater number of directors required to vote in favor`)
             ELSE JUST TRUE))

§ `Section 141(j): the board of a nonstock corporation`

-- "The certificate of incorporation of any nonstock corporation may provide that less than 1/3 of the members of the governing
-- body may constitute a quorum thereof and may otherwise provide that the business and affairs of the corporation shall be
-- managed in a manner different from that provided in this section."
-- For a stock corporation the floor of one third in subsection (b) stands, so the answer is FALSE; for a nonstock corporation
-- only the certificate (not the bylaws) may go below it.
-- src:375 | The certificate of incorporation of any nonstock corporation may provide that less than 1/3 of the members of the governing body may constitute a quorum thereof and may otherwise provide that the business and affairs of the corporation shall be managed in a manner different from that provided in this section. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 141(j) (src:375)
GIVEN `the kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation`
      `where the smaller quorum is provided` IS A `Where a provision is made`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 141(j) a quorum of less than one third of the members of the governing body may be provided` `the kind of corporation` `where the smaller quorum is provided` MEANS
        `the kind is a nonstock corporation` `the kind of corporation`
    AND `where the smaller quorum is provided` EQUALS `in the certificate of incorporation`

-- src:375 | and may otherwise provide that the business and affairs of the corporation shall be managed in a manner different from that provided in this section. …
@ref 8 Del. C. § 141(j) (src:375)
GIVEN `the kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation`
      `where the different manner of management is provided` IS A `Where a provision is made`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 141(j) the business and affairs may be managed in a different manner` `the kind of corporation` `where the different manner of management is provided` MEANS
        `the kind is a nonstock corporation` `the kind of corporation`
    AND `where the different manner of management is provided` EQUALS `in the certificate of incorporation`

-- The deeming rule of the second sentence: in section 141 as applied to a nonstock corporation, a reference to the board, to a
-- member of it, to stockholders, and to stock is read as follows, "Except as may be otherwise provided by the certificate".
DECLARE `s 141(j) Reference in section 141` IS ONE OF
    `a reference in section 141 to the board of directors`
    `a reference in section 141 to a member of the board of directors`
    `a reference in section 141 to stockholders`
    `a reference in section 141 to stock, capital stock, or shares thereof`

DECLARE `s 141(j) How a reference is read for a nonstock corporation` IS ONE OF
    `the governing body of the corporation, under s 141(j)`
    `a member of the governing body of the corporation, under s 141(j)`
    `the members of the corporation, under s 141(j)`
    `memberships of a nonprofit nonstock corporation, under s 141(j)`
    `membership interests of a nonstock corporation that is not a nonprofit nonstock corporation, under s 141(j)`

-- src:375 | Except as may be otherwise provided by the certificate of incorporation, this section shall apply to such a corporation, and when so applied, all references to the board of directors, to members thereof, and to stockholders shall be deemed to refer to the governing body of the corporation, the members thereof and the members of the corporation, respectively; and all references to stock, capital stock, or shares thereof shall be deemed to refer to memberships of a nonprofit nonstock corporation and to membership interests of any other nonstock corporation.
@ref 8 Del. C. § 141(j) (src:375)
GIVEN `the reference` IS A `s 141(j) Reference in section 141`
      `the kind of corporation` IS A `Kind of corporation`
      `the certificate of incorporation provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE `s 141(j) How a reference is read for a nonstock corporation`
`s 141(j) how a reference in section 141 is read` `the reference` `the kind of corporation` `the certificate of incorporation provides otherwise` MEANS
    IF   (NOT (`the kind is a nonstock corporation` `the kind of corporation`)) OR `the certificate of incorporation provides otherwise`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE CONSIDER `the reference`
         WHEN `a reference in section 141 to the board of directors` THEN JUST `the governing body of the corporation, under s 141(j)`
         WHEN `a reference in section 141 to a member of the board of directors` THEN JUST `a member of the governing body of the corporation, under s 141(j)`
         WHEN `a reference in section 141 to stockholders` THEN JUST `the members of the corporation, under s 141(j)`
         WHEN `a reference in section 141 to stock, capital stock, or shares thereof` THEN
             IF   `the kind is a nonprofit nonstock corporation` `the kind of corporation`
             THEN JUST `memberships of a nonprofit nonstock corporation, under s 141(j)`
             ELSE JUST `membership interests of a nonstock corporation that is not a nonprofit nonstock corporation, under s 141(j)`
